WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.330
We brought 150 devils in from the wild.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.740
They are placed across a number of zoos
and wildlife parks,

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.059
large free-range enclosures where devils
can live in a semi-natural environment

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:19.200
but still at much higher density than they do in the wild, breed up and live in a natural state.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.100
These are all components of what we call an insurance population

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.000
and it's an insurance meta-population -
there are many small populations.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.100
So if the disease gets
into one, we can still save the Tasmanian devil in others.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.400
The point of the devil insurance program

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.090
and Devil Ark, is to keep devils safe in captivity

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.300
before they're released to the wild, when deemed necessary.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:50.700
Now, one of the most critical components
of that is that devils remain as wild devils, behaviourally. 

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.200
That we can take a devil from Devil Ark,

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:55.610
put it back into the Tasmanian
wilderness and it survives

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.200
it knows how to find food, it knows how to
breed,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.600
it knows where water is, it knows how to find shelter.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.420
It's critical that we retain those wild behaviours.

